Toyota's new pro ace verso MPV now has  more to offer the van is not only  available in two versions it also comes  in three different body lengths ranging  between four point six and five point  three meters  didn't home car tester on delayed  cinnamon praises the interior which he  says meets passenger car standards he  has a slight beef with the position of  the bottle holders though their  dashboard location means he has to lean  forward to reach them he says putting  them in the door would have been more  practical recently sent for Lego phone  one very practical aspect is the  relatively slender body width of 1.92  with a turning circle of 11 meters this  vehicle is highly maneuverable in city  traffic  the Toyotas front is reminiscent of its  German rivals from VW and Mercedes the  compact version we tested has eight  seats and is 4.6 meters long with a  wheelbase of 2.9 meters that makes the  pro-ice vessel the shortest van in its  segment off the hook Andre says a ride  in the back is an experience worth  having  not only do passengers have room in all  directions but the design concept  includes large windows his favorite  feature is the panoramic roof making a  drive around the city a real sightseeing  tour the driver's seat is definitely not  that of a typical van the Toyota pro ace  van has 110 kilowatts of power giving it  a maximum speed of 170 kilometers an  hour the sprint from 0 to 100 takes 11  seconds the vehicle consumes an average  of 5 point 3 liters of fuel per 100  kilometers  the priceless Andre describes the  pro-ice vessel as easy to maneuver with  effortless steering but he finds the  gearbox action a bit rough shifting  could be smoother as far as he's  concerned but it's precise mr [ __ ]  I'm light vans are becoming more and  more popular on the European market and  the pro ways can rival the best of them  mr. David Andre says the three body  links and the choice of station wagon or  platform cab versions mean the pro ace  is poaching not only in VW's t6 hunting  grounds but also taking on the smaller  VW Caddy as well at heights of less than  1.9 meters the Pro ace is no problem for  underground or multi-story garages and  the low price makes it a real  alternative to the leading brands
 

